# Keyed.value: a request's carried value, sent once, never stored (protocol/client.md, 5).
# Dependencies replace the whole list: newly named tasks are added, omitted tasks removed (tasks.md, 7).
# The description's 512 bytes are MODEL_DESCRIPTION_BYTES (configuration.md, 6).
# The task's next-run wait, with source deadlines already translated to wall time.
# Shared admission vocabulary precedes the task wait that reuses it.
# Remaining documents and stream (protocol/client.md, 3 and 7).
# Account deadlines follow the optional-wall contract (rulings 190 and 191).
# Account changes share the account documents' payer type and ACCOUNT_USES bound.
# Small store (protocol/client.md, 10); TableEntry.request has Keyed.request's ceiling.
# A read value preserves the contract variant as well as its existing document (ruling 208).
# Chips.rows and OwnerInbox.needs/updates/selection: jig_client_view::Limits::document_bytes; each item is a length-prefixed piece (rulings 182 and 184).
# A delivery preserves its contract variant and the whole document (ruling 211).
